{"pageProps":{"note":{"id":"c3q8elwofwhu8p6uuv8dpcy","title":"Dimensions","desc":"","updated":1782289712071,"created":1782289251838,"custom":{},"fname":"random-markov-field.changes.dimensions","type":"note","vault":{"fsPath":".","selfContained":true,"name":"acol-dws"},"contentHash":"0d20b8b5f4ab7f6b1900ebdc579c6b11","links":[],"anchors":{},"children":[],"parent":"gwmhhu4cpb6qa0xcshsxw7l","data":{}},"body":"<h1 id=\"dimensions\">Dimensions<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#dimensions\"></a></h1>\n<p>With Andreas we changed the possible number of dimensions in the model. Before we allowed as many dimensions as we wanted, but now we have reduced it to only 2. </p>\n<p>This allowed us to change the way we store the Y data in the model and make it more efficient. It is now a doubly sparse matrix which allows us to quickly extract columns or rows from it.</p>","noteIndex":{"id":"3rbfqqbp7pwbkdcrgc97u7l","title":"Anticipated Chemistry of Life","desc":"","updated":1727785927929,"created":1671985562294,"custom":{"nav_order":0,"permalink":"/"},"fname":"root","type":"note","vault":{"fsPath":".","selfContained":true,"name":"acol-dws"},"contentHash":"f1947bd87c177e8ee5739c542c5dc574","links":[],"anchors":{"welcome-to-the-dendron-of-the-anticipated-chemistry-of-life":{"type":"header","text":"Welcome to the Dendron of the Anticipated Chemistry of Life","value":"welcome-to-the-dendron-of-the-anticipated-chemistry-of-life","line":8,"column":0,"depth":1}},"children":["l03fwlci5f5rdpot3v7oli6","6ddztf3hennsvej0xmrl90v","zxc3pre92d542wg70hmdhgl","0r3foyjkhoscuvks561fn42","8d14aky2v2izw8vum4zfg2i","hf5razdbb2dykm19x4p7p4m","gl0fpqrrok3wa7pzzc2820s","nnbrqied1xqexkjugy6ta13"],"parent":null,"data":{},"body":"\n# Welcome to the Dendron of the Anticipated Chemistry of Life\n\nThis dendron has the purpose to serve as a laboratory notebook for my PhD thesis. It will contain all the notes that I will take during my research as well as some results of the experim